<% content_for :title, "Help" %>

<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Help</h1>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Getting Started</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Trello is a simple task manager. Create boards for your projects, add lists for stages, and cards for individual tasks.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Creating a Board</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Click "New Board" in the top navigation. Give it a name and optional description.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Managing Lists</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Inside a board, use the "Add list" form to create columns (e.g., To Do, In Progress, Done). Lists are ordered left to right.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Managing Cards</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Click the "Add card" input at the bottom of any list to create a new card. Cards can have a title and description.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Moving Cards</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Drag and drop cards between lists to change their status. Cards can also be reordered within the same list.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>
      <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li><kbd class="bg-gray-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">Ctrl+N</kbd> New board</li>
        <li><kbd class="bg-gray-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">/</kbd> Focus search</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>